{"term":"dispute","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6a709aa8f25558ecfd","definition":"An argument or disagreement; a failure to agree.","example":"But is not this dispute over the question whether we have free will or not very like a dispute that we might engage in over the color of a tree — whether it be green or blue?","pos":"noun","synonyms":["debate","quarrel"],"antonyms":["accord","agreement","assent","concord","concordance","harmony","resolution","solution","union"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84ac0bed21ad30107b","definition":"Verbal controversy or disagreement; altercation; debate.","example":"Addicted more / To contemplation and profound dispute.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","argy-bargy","altercation","contention","barney","bawl out","blue","bobbery","brawl","clash","conflict","controversy","debate","difference","ding-dong","disagreement","discordance","disharmony","disputation","dispute","dissonance","disunion","dustup","face-off","falling out","feud","fight","flite","hassle","issue","palaver","quarrel","quibble","row","spat","squabble","tangle","threap","tiff","wrangle"],"antonyms":["accord","agreement","assent","concord","concordance","harmony","resolution","solution","union"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:97ce0e95ba1e7966ba","definition":"To contend in argument; to argue against something maintained, upheld, or claimed, by another.","example":"\"Now, though thy thoughts are green and tender, as becometh one so young, yet are they those of a thinking brain, and in truth thou dost bring back to my mind certain of those old philosophers with whom in days bygone I have disputed at Athens, and at Becca in Arabia, for thou hast the same crabbed air and dusty look, as though thou hadst passed thy days in reading ill-writ Greek, and been stained dark with the grime of manuscripts.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute","disputability","disputably","indisputably","industrial dispute","nondisputing","redispute","undisputing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7360b01701fd3393a5","definition":"To make a subject of disputation; to argue pro and con; to discuss.","example":"Some residents disputed the proposal, saying it was based more on emotion than fact.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute","disputability","disputably","indisputably","industrial dispute","nondisputing","redispute","undisputing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cff3c60a89ce1a010b","definition":"To oppose by argument or assertion; to controvert; to express dissent or opposition to; to call into question; to deny the truth or validity of.","example":"to dispute assertions or arguments","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute","disputability","disputably","indisputably","industrial dispute","nondisputing","redispute","undisputing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f6d8905da67ceb493","definition":"To strive or contend about; to contest.","example":"to dispute the possession of the ground with the Spaniards","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute","disputability","disputably","indisputably","industrial dispute","nondisputing","redispute","undisputing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cee5a31ada7c911c02","definition":"To struggle against; to resist.","example":"Dispute it [grief] like a man.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless","dispute resolution","domestic dispute","interdispute","predispute","trade dispute","disputability","disputably","indisputably","industrial dispute","nondisputing","redispute","undisputing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/dɪˈspjuːt/"},"wordFamily":["beyond dispute","counterdispute","disputeless"